1
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:07,000
Priya Raman: Thanks everyone for joining. This is the scope check before we start the
pilot build.

2
00:00:07,400 --> 00:00:12,840
Priya Raman: Three things on the agenda. What changed since kickoff, anything new,
and open questions.

3
00:00:13,740 --> 00:00:17,740
Dana Whitcombe: I will start, because there is a change that matters.

4
00:00:18,340 --> 00:00:24,500
Dana Whitcombe: The early shift in Columbus moved. The first trucks now roll out at
5:30, not six.

5
00:00:25,700 --> 00:00:32,220
Lena Sorensen: That is right. We pulled it forward half an hour to catch the morning
rail yard drops.

6
00:00:32,720 --> 00:00:42,480
Lena Sorensen: So the route suggestions need to be ready by 5:00 a.m. instead of 5:30
a.m. Dispatchers need half an hour to review before the trucks roll.

7
00:00:43,280 --> 00:00:50,880
Tomás Ferreira: Just to be sure I have it right. At kickoff we wrote down 5:30 and you
are now saying 5:00?

8
00:00:52,280 --> 00:00:55,200
Lena Sorensen: Yes, 5:00. 5:30 does not work anymore.

9
00:00:55,600 --> 00:01:02,480
Priya Raman: Understood. That also pushes the planning run earlier, so we will have
to revisit the 4:15 start time.

10
00:01:03,380 --> 00:01:10,980
Tomás Ferreira: At the current start time we would have 45 minutes, and the run takes
around 50 on a busy day.

11
00:01:11,580 --> 00:01:19,540
Priya Raman: So the start time has to move or the run has to get faster. I will not
pretend that is free.

12
00:01:20,740 --> 00:01:23,660
Dana Whitcombe: Fine. Just tell us what it costs.

13
00:01:24,160 --> 00:01:26,720
Priya Raman: Okay. Next, anything new since kickoff?

14
00:01:27,520 --> 00:01:36,200
Lena Sorensen: Yes, one new thing. Dispatchers need to pin a driver to a specific load,
and the assistant has to plan around the pin.

15
00:01:37,600 --> 00:01:43,760
Lena Sorensen: Some customers ask for a named driver, and today the dispatchers just
have to remember that.

16
00:01:44,160 --> 00:01:51,760
Tomás Ferreira: So a pin is a hard constraint for the planner. That is clear enough to
write down as a requirement.

17
00:01:52,660 --> 00:01:56,660
Priya Raman: Agreed. Now Dayton. Lena, where are we with the cross-dock?

18
00:01:57,260 --> 00:02:02,340
Lena Sorensen: Ignore what I said about October. The Dayton cross-dock slipped to next
spring.

19
00:02:03,540 --> 00:02:08,980
Dana Whitcombe: That also takes the forty extra loads a day out of our planning numbers.

20
00:02:09,480 --> 00:02:12,400
Priya Raman: Noted. That one comes off the list.

21
00:02:13,200 --> 00:02:19,000
Priya Raman: Now FleetDesk access. For phase one we have read-only, and suggestions
go to a dashboard.

22
00:02:20,400 --> 00:02:27,280
Marcus Oyelaran: I need to push back on that. We never agreed that read-only access was
enough for the pilot.

23
00:02:27,680 --> 00:02:35,640
Marcus Oyelaran: What I said at kickoff was that I could live with it to begin with. That
is not the same thing.

24
00:02:36,540 --> 00:02:42,340
Priya Raman: I hear you. In my notes from the kickoff, we recorded phase one as
read-only.

25
00:02:42,940 --> 00:02:49,100
Tomás Ferreira: And I said it twice, that we pull loads and drivers and never write
anything back.

26
00:02:50,300 --> 00:03:00,420
Marcus Oyelaran: You did. And I said to begin with. If dispatchers have to retype every
assignment into FleetDesk, the pilot will not show the time savings Dana
wants.

27
00:03:00,920 --> 00:03:04,200
Dana Whitcombe: He has a point. Retyping eats the savings.

28
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:11,160
Lena Sorensen: My team would not want to do the pilot if they have to type everything
twice.

29
00:03:12,560 --> 00:03:19,800
Priya Raman: Okay. This is a disagreement and I do not want to paper over it. Marcus,
what is your position?

30
00:03:20,200 --> 00:03:26,720
Marcus Oyelaran: Write access for assignments only, behind a feature flag, approved by my
team under the integration policy.

31
00:03:27,620 --> 00:03:35,220
Priya Raman: We cannot settle that on this call. We will record it as disputed and
Tomás will draft options for you.

32
00:03:35,820 --> 00:03:37,420
Marcus Oyelaran: That is fair.

33
00:03:38,620 --> 00:03:42,980
Priya Raman: Different topic, the driver app. Lena, you flagged something about
Android?

34
00:03:43,480 --> 00:03:50,720
Lena Sorensen: Yes. About fifteen percent of our owner-operator drivers carry phones
that are not Android. They bring their own devices.

35
00:03:51,520 --> 00:03:58,400
Tomás Ferreira: That breaks the Android only assumption. We would need either a second
app build or a web fallback.

36
00:03:59,800 --> 00:04:03,440
Priya Raman: Let's not decide today. We will cost both options.

37
00:04:03,840 --> 00:04:13,600
Tomás Ferreira: One decision I do want to make now. For loads, we will poll the
FleetDesk REST API every five minutes instead of building a file drop.

38
00:04:14,500 --> 00:04:21,740
Tomás Ferreira: This depends on the REST API assumption from kickoff, so if that
assumption changes, this decision changes with it.

39
00:04:22,340 --> 00:04:27,060
Dana Whitcombe: With sixty requests a minute shared, polling every five minutes is fine.

40
00:04:28,260 --> 00:04:30,100
Priya Raman: Agreed. Let me recap.

41
00:04:30,600 --> 00:04:38,920
Priya Raman: Change one, route suggestions by 5:00. Change two, driver pins. Dayton
is off for now. Read-only is disputed. Android is under review.

42
00:04:39,720 --> 00:04:43,720
Tomás Ferreira: And the polling decision stands, subject to the API assumption.

43
00:04:45,120 --> 00:04:48,040
Dana Whitcombe: When do we get the revised plan?

44
00:04:48,440 --> 00:04:53,160
Priya Raman: By Friday. We will send the updated requirements and the confirmation
list.

45
00:04:54,060 --> 00:04:55,660
Dana Whitcombe: Good.

46
00:04:56,260 --> 00:05:02,420
Marcus Oyelaran: One more thing from me. Nothing new connects to our network without my
team approving it.

47
00:05:03,620 --> 00:05:06,900
Tomás Ferreira: Understood, that is already in the security notes.

48
00:05:07,400 --> 00:05:09,000
Priya Raman: Thanks everybody.

49
00:05:09,800 --> 00:05:11,400
Lena Sorensen: Thanks.
